# Remix Rules — GoodEpoch Cursor Rules Pack v1
# Applies to: Remix v2+ / React Router v7 (framework mode)
# Stack: Remix/RRv7, React 19, TypeScript 5.5+

## Mental Model: Web Standards First

- Remix is built on Web APIs — Request/Response/FormData/URL, not abstractions over them
- Think in HTTP: every route handles requests and returns responses
- Progressive enhancement is the goal: forms work without JS, JS enhances the experience
- Loaders run on server only. Actions run on server only. Components can run on both.

## Route Conventions (Remix v2 flat file routing)

```
app/
  routes/
    _index.tsx              # / (home)
    users.tsx               # /users layout
    users._index.tsx        # /users index
    users.$userId.tsx       # /users/:userId
    users.$userId.edit.tsx  # /users/:userId/edit
    users_.new.tsx          # /users/new (breaks out of users layout)
    _auth.login.tsx         # /login (no auth layout prefix in URL)
    _auth.tsx               # auth layout wrapper
```

## Loaders — Data Fetching

- Every route that needs data exports a `loader`:
  ```typescript
  import { json, type LoaderFunctionArgs } from '@remix-run/node'
  import { useLoaderData } from '@remix-run/react'
  
  export async function loader({ params, request }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
    const user = await getUserById(params.userId)
    if (!user) throw new Response('Not Found', { status: 404 })
    return json({ user })
  }
  
  export default function UserPage() {
    const { user } = useLoaderData<typeof loader>()  // fully typed
    return <div>{user.name}</div>
  }
  ```
- Never fetch in components — always use loaders
- `throw new Response()` for HTTP errors — they're caught by error boundaries
- Use `defer()` for non-critical data that can load after initial render

## Actions — Mutations

- Every form mutation uses an `action` function, not an API endpoint:
  ```typescript
  import { redirect, type ActionFunctionArgs } from '@remix-run/node'
  
  export async function action({ request, params }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
    const formData = await request.formData()
    const name = formData.get('name')
    
    const result = updateUserSchema.safeParse({ name, id: params.userId })
    if (!result.success) {
      return json({ errors: result.error.flatten() }, { status: 400 })
    }
    
    await updateUser(result.data)
    return redirect(`/users/${params.userId}`)
  }
  ```
- Return errors from actions, throw for HTTP errors
- Always redirect after successful POST (PRG pattern)
- Use `intent` hidden field for routes with multiple actions

## Forms — Progressive Enhancement

- Native `<Form>` from Remix for all mutations:
  ```typescript
  import { Form, useNavigation, useActionData } from '@remix-run/react'
  
  export default function EditUser() {
    const errors = useActionData<typeof action>()
    const navigation = useNavigation()
    const isSubmitting = navigation.state === 'submitting'
    
    return (
      <Form method="post">
        <input name="name" />
        {errors?.fieldErrors.name && <p>{errors.fieldErrors.name}</p>}
        <button disabled={isSubmitting}>
          {isSubmitting ? 'Saving...' : 'Save'}
        </button>
      </Form>
    )
  }
  ```
- `useFetcher` for forms that don't navigate (inline editing, likes, etc.)
- `fetcher.Form` for non-navigating mutations

## Authentication

- Session-based auth preferred over JWT in Remix (server renders, no token management):
  ```typescript
  // lib/session.ts
  import { createCookieSessionStorage } from '@remix-run/node'
  
  export const { getSession, commitSession, destroySession } =
    createCookieSessionStorage({
      cookie: {
        name: '__session',
        httpOnly: true,
        secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',
        sameSite: 'lax',
        secrets: [process.env.SESSION_SECRET!],
      }
    })
  ```
- Auth check in loaders: `if (!user) throw redirect('/login')`
- `requireUser` helper that throws redirect if not authenticated

## Error Boundaries

- Every route should have an `ErrorBoundary`:
  ```typescript
  export function ErrorBoundary() {
    const error = useRouteError()
    if (isRouteErrorResponse(error)) {
      return <div>HTTP {error.status}: {error.data}</div>
    }
    return <div>Unexpected error: {error.message}</div>
  }
  ```
- Errors bubble up to the nearest ErrorBoundary — fine-grained control

## Meta and SEO

```typescript
import type { MetaFunction } from '@remix-run/node'

export const meta: MetaFunction<typeof loader> = ({ data }) => [
  { title: data?.user.name ?? 'User' },
  { name: 'description', content: `Profile of ${data?.user.name}` },
  { property: 'og:title', content: data?.user.name },
]
```

## Performance

- Loaders run in parallel automatically — nested route loaders fetch concurrently
- `prefetch="intent"` on `<Link>` for hover-intent prefetching
- `defer()` + `<Await>` for streaming slow data without blocking render
- HTTP caching headers in loader responses: `Cache-Control: private, max-age=300`
